## vendored / patched copy

This directory is a PATCHED COPY of upstream burn-rs/cubecl
(https://github.com/burn-rs/cubecl) — crates `cubecl-runtime`, `cubecl-server`
and `cubecl-cuda` at 0.11.0-pre.4 — redistributed under the same dual license
as upstream (MIT OR Apache-2.0, per each crate's `Cargo.toml`).

The upstream copyright notice above is retained deliberately. MIT section (a)
and Apache-2.0 section 4 both require it, and this copy was previously stamped
"Copyright (c) 2026 sehaxe", which was wrong: it is upstream code we patch, not
code we wrote.

Patches applied by dormouse:

- `cubecl-runtime`, `cubecl-server` — the stale-page #1401 fix to the memory
  pools. The pools moved to `cubecl-server` upstream in 0.11.0-pre.4, so the
  fix lives there now.
- `cubecl-cuda` — no local patch; carried so the vendored unit is one tree and
  the root `[patch.crates-io]` has one path per crate.

The repository as a whole is MIT (see the root `LICENSE`, owner decision
2026-10-01). These vendored directories keep their upstream terms — MIT **or**
Apache-2.0 for the cubecl crates, which is what the per-crate `LICENSE-MIT` /
`LICENSE-APACHE` files state — and the root `vendor/dormouse-fused/LICENSE` scope
note describes that vendored unit.
